# Never sent to the Docker daemon as part of this image's build context --
# see lessons/02-dockerfiles-layers-and-caching.md's ".dockerignore" section
# for exactly what "build context" means and why this file matters even
# for things the Dockerfile never explicitly COPYs.

# Real secrets and machine-specific local config -- environment variables
# are supplied at container-run time instead, via docker-compose.yml's
# own `environment:` block, never baked into the image itself.
.env
.env.test

# Local virtual environments -- this image installs dependencies fresh,
# inside the build, via requirements.txt; a locally-created .venv would
# be a large, host-OS-specific folder with zero use inside a Linux
# container, and copying it in by accident would also risk shipping
# whatever secrets a local .env-based tool might have cached inside it.
.venv/
.venv-*/

# Python bytecode caches and pytest's own cache -- regenerated
# automatically, never meaningful to ship.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Test code -- this app's tests/ folder is real and valuable, but it has
# no reason to exist inside the image that actually serves production
# traffic; keeping it out of the build context also keeps this image
# from accidentally depending on requirements-dev.txt-only packages
# (pytest, ruff) that were deliberately never installed into this image
# at all. See lessons/07-containerizing-questlogs-backend.md.
tests/

# Version control metadata -- never relevant inside a container.
.git/
.gitignore
